          "outlet_id": "gbnews",
          "published_at": 1790694052,
          "summary": "The police watchdog has found no evidence of \"tactical contact\" ahead of a crash along the A66 which killed two officers. Seven people died in the collision in the early hours of August 22 after a Volkswagen Passat drove the wrong way down the busy A-road near Middlesbrough. The probe did not find any use of a stinger ahead of the incident, the Independent Office for Police Conduct added. PC Tom Clough, 38, and PC Matthew Blades, 37, died in the collision which sent shockwaves through the local community…",
